When the X11 window under the pointer is destroyed (a menu, a tooltip, a
closed chat), count the pointer as having left it: the compositor can't send
a leave for a surface that is gone, so pointer_enter_count stayed above zero
for good.  From then on, while the pointer was over Wayland windows, the X
pointer stayed over whichever X11 window was at its last position, and mouse
buttons the compositor forwarded for push to talk (cosmic-comp's
xwayland_eavesdropping.pointer) went to that window -- Steam's, say --
instead of the root window, where Discord listens.

(An earlier version replaced the count by "a window has the pointer"
altogether; that also counted the pointer as gone in other cases.)

--- a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-window.c
+++ b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-window.c
@@ -1696,8 +1696,15 @@
     compUnredirectWindow(serverClient, window, CompositeRedirectManual);
 
     xorg_list_for_each_entry(xwl_seat, &xwl_screen->seat_list, link) {
-        if (xwl_seat->focus_window == xwl_window)
+        if (xwl_seat->focus_window == xwl_window) {
             xwl_seat->focus_window = NULL;
+            /* The compositor can't send a leave for this surface, which is
+             * going away: count it as left, or pointer_enter_count stays
+             * above zero for good, and the sprite no longer leaves X11
+             * windows when the pointer moves to Wayland ones. */
+            if (xwl_seat->pointer_enter_count > 0)
+                xwl_seat->pointer_enter_count--;
+        }
         if (xwl_seat->tablet_focus_window == xwl_window)
             xwl_seat->tablet_focus_window = NULL;
         if (xwl_seat->last_focus_window == xwl_window)
